# Repo Root Resolution

- Runtime code must not search for the repository root.
- Do not hardcode `../../..`-style climbs, `new URL('../../...')`, or similar manual path math to locate the repository root in application code.
- If root lookup is unavoidable, use a shared repo utility from this monorepo (if one exists) or confine lookup to tooling, build scripts, tests, and generators that already start from an explicit directory.
- If runtime code needs repository-relative paths, establish that contract at startup or through explicit configuration instead of looking up the root during request handling.
